4. Initial Paper Prototype

For our initial paper prototype, we decided to take inspiration from the board game Snakes and Ladders.

The prototype uses a grid-based movement system in which players navigate a series of tiles containing different obstacles and special effects.

The objective is to reach the finish while avoiding hazards and dealing with the rising lava.
Core Game Rules

    All players begin at the START position.
    Players roll a six-sided dice to determine how many spaces they can move.
    Players can move up, down, left, or right.
    Certain obstacles prevent movement or apply special effects when encountered.
    After all players have taken their turns, the lava rises by one row.
    Players caught by the lava lose their current life. During initial testing, each player has one life. If caught, they are returned to the top of the board to attempt the challenge again.
    The first player to reach the FINISH position wins.

Obstacle Effects
Obstacle	Effect
 Lightning Bolt	Stuns the player, preventing them from moving during their next turn.
 Fire	Sends the player back one tile.
 Ladder	Moves the player upwards to a designated tile, usually one row higher.
Trapdoor	Drops the player down by one row.
Jail	Traps the player for one full round, preventing movement.
Spikes	Instantly removes one of the player's lives when landed on.
5. Initial Design Considerations

The paper prototype is intended to help us experiment with the game's core movement and obstacle mechanics before implementing them digitally.

It allows us to test:

    Whether the rising lava creates enough urgency.
    Whether the obstacles provide interesting challenges.
    Whether players have enough opportunities to choose different routes.
    Whether the movement system feels fair and understandable.
    Whether the game is too easy or difficult to complete.

The results of these tests will help us refine the mechanics and determine how they should translate into the final game.
