LASTEST PAPER PROTOTYPE TEST 11/20/2026

Friday Changes and Game Testing Report
Changes Made

    Added More Spikes: Increased the number of spikes throughout the map to create more obstacles and challenges for players.
    Spin the Wheel: Replaced the four-sided dice with a spinning wheel to determine how many spaces players move.
    Exact Number Required: Players must now land on the exact number needed to reach the finish line. They cannot move past it.
    Jail Rule: Players who land in jail must now miss two rounds before they can continue playing.
    Expanded Map: Increased the map size to 7 rows and 8 columns, creating a larger playing area.
    Additional Traps: Added more traps to fill the expanded map and maintain the game's difficulty.
    Rising Lava: When a player spins the wheel and lands on the lava space, the lava level rises, adding another challenge to the game.
    Instead of taking place inside a Lab, the game will take place in a ruined temple, with rising lava.

Game Testing

These changes were made to improve the gameplay by adding more obstacles, increasing the difficulty, and making the game more exciting. The expanded map and new spinning wheel mechanic also introduce more variety and unpredictability.


